Bitwise Operator

    1. Bitwise & (OR operator)
        if both are 1 then output is 1, otherwise it is 0;

    2. Bitwise | (AND operator)
        if anyone is 1, then it is 1, otherwise it is 0;

    3. Bitwise ^ (XOR operator)
        if both are same, then it is 0, otherwise it is 1.

    4. Bitwise << (left shift)
        10 << 2 means in the binary number of the 10, every binary digits shift left two positions. 

        Actually this operator do a small operation (a << b), a * pow(2, b)

    5. Bitwise >> (right shift)
        10 >> 2 means shifting two binary digits to right. But keep in mind that there is no space for shifted binary at the right end since it was the last digit.

        Actually this operator do a small operation (a >> b),  a/pow(2, b)

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Operator Precedence
Answer: This tells the compiler to do the solving as per the priority order of the operators.

Scope of Variables
    1. Local
    2. Global

Data Type Modifier
Answer: Changing the meaning of the data types.
    1. Unsigned
    2. Signed
    3. Short
    4. Long
    5. long long


